What was acheived?

1. Linux VM Installation

Installed Ubuntu Linux in a virtual machine and used the terminal to perform basic Linux operations.

2. GCC Configuration

Configured GCC for compiling C programs. Verified the installation using gcc --version and compiled a basic C program.

3. Git Repository Setup

Created a Git repository for the project using git init. Added project files and created the initial commit.

4. Project Structure

Created a basic project structure containing source files, header files, a Makefile, and a README file.

5. Shell Architecture

Understood the role of the shell as an interface between the user and the Linux kernel. The shell accepts commands from the user and requests the kernel to perform the required operations.

6. Makefile

Created an initial Makefile to automate the compilation of the C program. Used make to build the program and make clean to remove generated files.

7. Process Abstraction

A process is a program that is currently executing. Each process has a unique Process ID (PID) and uses system resources such as CPU and memory.

8. fork()

Studied the fork() system call, which creates a new child process from the existing parent process. After fork(), both the parent and child processes continue execution.

9. exec()

Studied the exec() family of system calls. exec() replaces the current program with another program while continuing to use the same process.

10. Parent-Child Relationship

Observed the relationship between parent and child processes using PID and PPID. The child process is created by the parent using fork().


11. System Call Tracing

Used strace to observe the system calls made by a program. System calls such as execve, write, and exit can be observed during program execution.

12. Process Monitoring

Used ps to view running processes, top to monitor processes and resource usage in real time, and /proc to view detailed information about individual processes.
